125:Ta38,Visit us from **8–15 October 2025 in Düsseldorf | Hall 7, Stand 70SU-04**

*Waldems, October 202***5** – plastship will be exhibiting at [**K 2025 in Düsseldorf**,](https://www.k-online.de/en/Home/The_World_s_No._1_Trade_Fair_for_Plastics_and_Rubber?ticket=15533055595138) the world’s leading trade fair for the plastics and rubber industry. Under the motto *“Green – Smart – Responsible”*, the focus is on the transformation towards a sustainable, digital circular economy. With our participation, we will showcase practical solutions that enable businesses to use recycled plastics efficiently, transparently and with assured quality.

## IN FOCUS: KISS – AI-driven flow stream optimisation

With the [**KISS-Projekt**](/benchmark/) (“AI-based Qualification, Control and Optimisation of Material Flows”), plastship presents a modular, data-driven platform. It enables companies to accurately analyse material flows and improve the use of recyclates – from optical and mechanical tests to chemical analyses.\
KISS combines AI, digital tools and material data to standardise and advance the use of recycled plastics across Europe.

## OUR SOLUTIONS FOR EFFICIENT RECYCLED MATERIAL USE

**- Recyclate sourcing & partnerships:** Access to verified materials and trusted collaborations.\
\- **Material qualification & benchmarking:** Transparent and comparable assessment of recyclates along the supply chain.\
\- **Digital flow stream optimisation:** Data-driven analyses and recommendations for more efficient plastics utilisation.\
\- **Practical collaboration:** Support for integrating recyclates into products and packaging – together with partners such as [RIGK](https://www.rigk.de/en/).

![](/images/cms/plastship-grafik-youtube-format-fbb95c.webp)

## MEET OUR TEAM ON SITE

Visitors can receive individual advice and experience first-hand how AI and digital tools support the plastics circular economy.

> With KISS and our core services, we demonstrate how companies can use recyclates efficiently, transparently and with high quality.

says our **Managing Director Andreas Bastian,**

> We bring together data, technology and practical expertise to sustainably strengthen the circular economy in Europe.

### K 2025

🗓 8–15 October 2025\
📍 Hall 7, Stand 70SU-04\
[**👉 Book your appointment now and secure your entry code**](mailto:bastian@plastship.com)

If you have questions or suggestions, please contact me!

**Mirco Gattinger**, Marketing & Social Media Manager\
